8.3.1. Generics # C# collection types use generics : a type in angle brackets after a class name tells the compiler what element type the collection holds. The generic collection types live in the System.Collections.Generic namespace, which some project templates import through implicit usings. Include using System.Collections.Generic; when those imports are not enabled. The generic list syntax is: List < T > To create a list, supply a type argument for the elements it will store: The declaration and construction patterns are: List<elementType> name = new List<elementType>();
